  why:
    'Five of these six parts are the same gesture — make a thing in the Project window, then ' +
    'drag it into a slot — and that gesture is the whole reason ScriptableObjects exist: data ' +
    'a designer can author without a programmer. The split matters because the halves fail ' +
    'differently. Parts one to four need no code at all, so a card with a name, a number and a ' +
    'picture is finished without opening a script. Part five is the only one that costs a ' +
    'programmer, and it only appears when you invent a field the class does not already have.',
